<title>USA: CMS Energy unit signs contract in Thailand.</title>
<headline>CMS Energy unit signs contract in Thailand.</headline>
<dateline>DEARBORN, Mich. 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>CMS Energy Corp said Wednesday its CMS Generation Co subsidiary signed a contract with Thailand's  AMATA-EGCO Power Ltd to operate and maintain a natural gas-fueled cogeneration plant.</p>
<p>The plant is currently under construction at the Bang Pakong II Industrial Park near Bangkok, it added.</p>
<p>The facility is expected to be completed in 1998.</p>
<p>The company said the plant marks CMS Generation's entrance into Thailand's energy market.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
